From: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shared/shell: print in non-interactive mode again

bt_shell_printf() returns early when no input is attached, but
non-interactive mode (bluetoothctl <command>) never attaches one, so
every non-interactive command printed nothing (bluez 5.86 on EROS Q:
`bluetoothctl show` -> empty, rc 0).  bt_audio_up.sh polls
`bluetoothctl show | grep Powered:` after starting bluetoothd, so it
timed out and exited before starting bluealsa.

---
--- a/src/shared/shell.c	2026-10-03 22:13:11.653237663 +0000
+++ b/src/shared/shell.c	2026-10-03 22:13:11.667429926 +0000
@@ -711,9 +711,10 @@
 	char *saved_line;
 	int saved_point;
 
-	if (queue_isempty(data.inputs))
-		return;
-
+	/* Non-interactive mode never attaches an input (bt_shell_attach
+	 * runs the command instead), so check it before the empty-inputs
+	 * bail-out -- otherwise `bluetoothctl show` etc. print nothing.
+	 */
 	if (data.mode == MODE_NON_INTERACTIVE) {
 		va_start(args, fmt);
 		vprintf(fmt, args);
@@ -721,6 +722,9 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
+	if (queue_isempty(data.inputs))
+		return;
+
 	save_input = !RL_ISSTATE(RL_STATE_DONE);
 
 	if (save_input) {
